faqsText:
Are plots available for sale in Faisal Town Islamabad? | Yes. There is active plot inventory in both Faisal Town Phase 1/F-18 and Faisal Town Phase 2/FT-II, although the two projects should be compared separately.

What is the difference between Phase 1 and Phase 2 plots? | Phase 1 is an established block-based resale market, while Phase 2 is a newer sector-based project with booking, installment and resale inventory.

Which blocks are in Faisal Town Phase 1? | Phase 1 includes Block A, Block B, Block B-1 and Block C. Blocks A, B and C currently have strong visible resale inventory. :contentReference[oaicite:10]{index=10}

What plot sizes are available in Faisal Town Phase 1? | Common sizes range from approximately 5 marla to 1 kanal, although available sizes vary by block.

What sectors can I compare in Faisal Town Phase 2? | Current detailed guides on this website cover Sector O, Sector P, Sector R, Sector S, Sector T and Overseas Enclave.

What is the price of an 8-marla Phase 1 plot? | Current Block B asking examples range roughly from PKR 1.48 crore to above PKR 1.8 crore, while other blocks and special locations may differ. :contentReference[oaicite:11]{index=11}

What is the price of a 5-marla Block C plot? | Current Block C asking examples appear around roughly PKR 1.15 crore to PKR 1.5 crore depending on exact location and plot characteristics. :contentReference[oaicite:12]{index=12}

What is the price of a Phase 2 Sector O plot? | Current seller listings include approximately PKR 27.9 lakh for 5.56 marla, PKR 37.3 lakh for 8 marla and PKR 48.5 lakh for about 10.89 marla under some cash offers. Verify current availability and terms before booking. :contentReference[oaicite:13]{index=13}

Are Phase 2 plots available on installments? | Some Phase 2 inventory is offered under installment structures, while other inventory is cash or resale. Check the exact sector and property because terms differ.

Should I visit the plot before buying? | Yes. Match the documents and map to the actual site and inspect access, road width, development and surrounding conditions before substantial payment.
